), add `kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional()`, `policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional()` and `ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional()`. Leave `command` and `.strict()` as they are. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH` prints the three new lines.\n-- [ ] T008 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendation` (`$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`), add `readonly command?: string`, `readonly policy?: string` and `readonly ownerSkillId?: string`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` dictionaries from `PY`. Verify: `rg -n \"HAND_AUTHORED\" $ADV --glob '!dist'` prints nothing, `python3 -m py_compile $PY` exits 0 and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T010 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, change `readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;` to `readonly routingEnabled: boolean;` and the filter in `scoringCommandBridges` to `bridge.routingEnabled === true`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"readonly routingEnabled: boolean;\" $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints one line.\n-- [ ] T011 [P] In `rankShippedFleet` (`RC`), set `hit` true when `shipped[0].skillId === hub` or `shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub`, and set `present` true when any shipped entry has `skillId === hub` or `ownerSkillId === hub`. Change nothing else. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0 and prints `[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed`.\n+- [x] T006 [P] In `CA`, add `export interface CommandRow { readonly command: string; readonly policy?: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string }`, an empty marked block `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` holding `export const COMMAND_ROWS: Readonly<Record<string, CommandRow>> = {};` and `export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {};` then `// END GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, and `export function commandRowFor(id: string): CommandRow | undefined` that reads `COMMAND_ROWS` with `Object.hasOwn`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"GENERATED COMMAND ROWS\" $CA` prints 2.\n+- [x] T007 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` (`SCH`), add `kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional()`, `policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional()` and `ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional()`. Leave `command` and `.strict()` as they are. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH` prints the three new lines.\n+- [x] T008 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendation` (`$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`), add `readonly command?: string`, `readonly policy?: string` and `readonly ownerSkillId?: string`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` dictionaries from `PY`. Verify: `rg -n \"HAND_AUTHORED\" $ADV --glob '!dist'` prints nothing, `python3 -m py_compile $PY` exits 0 and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n+- [x] T010 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, change `readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;` to `readonly routingEnabled: boolean;` and the filter in `scoringCommandBridges` to `bridge.routingEnabled === true`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"readonly routingEnabled: boolean;\" $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints one line.\n+- [x] T011 [P] In `rankShippedFleet` (`RC`), set `hit` true when `shipped[0].skillId === hub` or `shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub`, and set `present` true when any shipped entry has `skillId === hub` or `ownerSkillId === hub`. Change nothing else. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0 and prints `[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed`.\n \n ### Wave 2\n-- [ ] T012 In `D`, add `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)` and register `CA`'s `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `generatedSources`. Emit one `COMMAND_ROWS` row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry: its TypeScript id, its Python id and its entry id. `command` is the doctor runnable string from `DOCTOR_DETAILS` or the entry's `command`. `policy` is the `commandPolicies` record whose route matches the runnable's target, or the route-null record. When the runnable names no target and the command has several route records, take the strictest of `ask`, `start` and `run`. `ownerSkillId` is the entry's `skillId`. Emit `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string the same way. Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -n \"'command-doctor-update': \\{ command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'command-speckit-search': \\{ command: '/speckit:search', policy: 'run'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'create:agent': \\{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'\" $CA` prints one line and `$TC` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T013 [P] In `recommendationFromCli` (`FB`), keep `value.kind` when it is `skill` or `command` (default `skill`), keep `value.policy` when it is `run`, `start` or `ask`, and keep `value.ownerSkillId` when it is a non-empty string. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n-- [ ] T014 [P] In `$ADV/tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts`, add one case that parses a recommendation with all four fields and one that rejects it with `consequence: 'x'` added. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n-- [ ] T015 [P] In `RT`, add two cases through the stand-in advisor: a `create:agent` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` first and `sk-doc` second counts as a hit for `--hub sk-doc`, and a `command-doctor-git-hooks` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-git'` first and `sk-doc` second still prints `outranked`. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0.\n+- [x] T012 In `D`, add `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)` and register `CA`'s `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `generatedSources`. Emit one `COMMAND_ROWS` row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry: its TypeScript id, its Python id and its entry id. `command` is the doctor runnable string from `DOCTOR_DETAILS` or the entry's `command`. `policy` is the `commandPolicies` record whose route matches the runnable's target, or the route-null record. When the runnable names no target and the command has several route records, take the strictest of `ask`, `start` and `run`. `ownerSkillId` is the entry's `skillId`. Emit `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string the same way. Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -n \"'command-doctor-update': \\{ command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'command-speckit-search': \\{ command: '/speckit:search', policy: 'run'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'create:agent': \\{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'\" $CA` prints one line and `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T013 [P] In `recommendationFromCli` (`FB`), keep `value.kind` when it is `skill` or `command` (default `skill`), keep `value.policy` when it is `run`, `start` or `ask`, and keep `value.ownerSkillId` when it is a non-empty string. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n+- [x] T014 [P] In `$ADV/tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts`, add one case that parses a recommendation with all four fields and one that rejects it with `consequence: 'x'` added. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n+- [x] T015 [P] In `RT`, add two cases through the stand-in advisor: a `create:agent` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` first and `sk-doc` second counts as a hit for `--hub sk-doc`, and a `command-doctor-git-hooks` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-git'` first and `sk-doc` second still prints `outranked`. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0.\n \n ### Wave 3\n-- [ ] T016 In `publicRecommendation` (`H`), add `kind: recommendation.kind`, and when `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)` returns a row, add its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"save context\"}' | jq '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:save\")] | length'` prints 1.\n-- [ ] T017 In `R`, render the label of a recommendation that has a command, from its fields or else from `commandRowFor(skill)`, as `<ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)`, dropping the parenthesis when no policy is known. Use it for the `use` head and both sides of the `ambiguous` head. Every part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`. Rewrite `doctorCommandString` to return `commandRowFor(id)?.command` for a doctor id. Leave the `Also:` line's trigger unchanged. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS\\[\" $R` prints nothing.\n-- [ ] T018 In `CLI`, pass the prompt to `degradedRecommendations` and export it. For an entry with a `commandRowFor(entry.skill)` row: when the prompt contains the row's bare slash command (the text before the first space), emit `skillId`, `kind: 'command'`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. Otherwise emit the row's `ownerSkillId` as `skillId` with `kind: 'skill'`, and drop it when that skill is already in the list. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T016 In `publicRecommendation` (`H`), add `kind: recommendation.kind`, and when `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)` returns a row, add its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"save context\"}' | jq '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:save\")] | length'` prints 1.\n+- [x] T017 In `R`, render the label of a recommendation that has a command, from its fields or else from `commandRowFor(skill)`, as `<ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)`, dropping the parenthesis when no policy is known. Use it for the `use` head and both sides of the `ambiguous` head. Every part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`. Rewrite `doctorCommandString` to return `commandRowFor(id)?.command` for a doctor id. Leave the `Also:` line's trigger unchanged. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS\\[\" $R` prints nothing.\n+- [x] T018 In `CLI`, pass the prompt to `degradedRecommendations` and export it. For an entry with a `commandRowFor(entry.skill)` row: when the prompt contains the row's bare slash command (the text before the first space), emit `skillId`, `kind: 'command'`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. Otherwise emit the row's `ownerSkillId` as `skillId` with `kind: 'skill'`, and drop it when that skill is already in the list. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n \n ### Wave 4\n-- [ ] T019 In `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`H`), build `alreadyOffered` from the `command` fields of the recommendations and delete `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID`. When a hub gets an attached command, also set `policy: COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` when that key exists. Verify: after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\",\"options\":{\"includeCompiledRoute\":true}}' | jq -c '.data.recommendations[0] | {skillId,command,policy}'` prints `{\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}`, and `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n-- [ ] T020 Delete `renderDoctorCommandStrings` and the `R` entry from `generatedSources` in `D`, then delete the `GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS` block from `R`, then run `node $D`. Verify: `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS|renderDoctorCommandStrings\" $D $R` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh` and `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T019 In `enrichCompiledRoutes` (`H`), build `alreadyOffered` from the `command` fields of the recommendations and delete `BRIDGE_COMMAND_BY_ID`. When a hub gets an attached command, also set `policy: COMMAND_POLICIES[command]` when that key exists. Verify: after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\",\"options\":{\"includeCompiledRoute\":true}}' | jq -c '.data.recommendations[0] | {skillId,command,policy}'` prints `{\"skillId\":\"sk-doc\",\"command\":\"/create:readme\",\"policy\":\"start\"}`, and `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n+- [x] T020 Delete `renderDoctorCommandStrings` and the `R` entry from `generatedSources` in `D`, then delete the `GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS` block from `R`, then run `node $D`. Verify: `rg -n \"GENERATED DOCTOR COMMANDS|renderDoctorCommandStrings\" $D $R` prints nothing, `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh` and `$TC` exits 0.\n \n ### Wave 5\n - [ ] T021 [P] Create `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`. It renders six constructed results through `renderAdvisorBrief` and asserts the six heads in `plan.md` section 3 exactly, that each head before `\\nDirectives:` is at most 320 characters and that no head contains `command-`. Add one row each for a missing field filled from `COMMAND_ROWS`, an id with no row and a missing policy. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md b/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md\nindex 7a58cad562..03b2722dbc 100644\n--- a/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md\n+++ b/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/005-recommendation-contract-and-brief/tasks.md\n@@ -77,27 +77,27 @@ Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. A\n ## Phase 2: Implementation\n \n ### Wave 1\n-- [ ] T006 [P] In `CA`, add `export interface CommandRow { readonly command: string; readonly policy?: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string }`, an empty marked block `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` holding `export const COMMAND_ROWS: Readonly<Record<string, CommandRow>> = {};` and `export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {};` then `// END GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, and `export function commandRowFor(id: string): CommandRow | undefined` that reads `COMMAND_ROWS` with `Object.hasOwn`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"GENERATED COMMAND ROWS\" $CA` prints 2.\n-- [ ] T007 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` (`SCH`), add `kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional()`, `policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional()` and `ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional()`. Leave `command` and `.strict()` as they are. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH` prints the three new lines.\n-- [ ] T008 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendation` (`$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`), add `readonly command?: string`, `readonly policy?: string` and `readonly ownerSkillId?: string`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` dictionaries from `PY`. Verify: `rg -n \"HAND_AUTHORED\" $ADV --glob '!dist'` prints nothing, `python3 -m py_compile $PY` exits 0 and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T010 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, change `readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;` to `readonly routingEnabled: boolean;` and the filter in `scoringCommandBridges` to `bridge.routingEnabled === true`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"readonly routingEnabled: boolean;\" $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints one line.\n-- [ ] T011 [P] In `rankShippedFleet` (`RC`), set `hit` true when `shipped[0].skillId === hub` or `shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub`, and set `present` true when any shipped entry has `skillId === hub` or `ownerSkillId === hub`. Change nothing else. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0 and prints `[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed`.\n+- [x] T006 [P] In `CA`, add `export interface CommandRow { readonly command: string; readonly policy?: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string }`, an empty marked block `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` holding `export const COMMAND_ROWS: Readonly<Record<string, CommandRow>> = {};` and `export const COMMAND_POLICIES: Readonly<Record<string, 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'>> = {};` then `// END GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, and `export function commandRowFor(id: string): CommandRow | undefined` that reads `COMMAND_ROWS` with `Object.hasOwn`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -c \"GENERATED COMMAND ROWS\" $CA` prints 2.\n+- [x] T007 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` (`SCH`), add `kind: z.enum(['skill', 'command']).optional()`, `policy: z.enum(['run', 'start', 'ask']).optional()` and `ownerSkillId: z.string().min(1).optional()`. Leave `command` and `.strict()` as they are. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"^  (kind|policy|ownerSkillId):\" $SCH` prints the three new lines.\n+- [x] T008 [P] In `AdvisorRecommendation` (`$ADV/lib/subprocess.ts`), add `readonly command?: string`, `readonly policy?: string` and `readonly ownerSkillId?: string`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T009 [P] Delete the `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGES` and `HAND_AUTHORED_COMMAND_BRIDGE_OWNER_NORMALIZATION` dictionaries from `PY`. Verify: `rg -n \"HAND_AUTHORED\" $ADV --glob '!dist'` prints nothing, `python3 -m py_compile $PY` exits 0 and `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py` exits 0.\n+- [x] T010 [P] In `$ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, change `readonly routingEnabled?: boolean;` to `readonly routingEnabled: boolean;` and the filter in `scoringCommandBridges` to `bridge.routingEnabled === true`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"readonly routingEnabled: boolean;\" $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints one line.\n+- [x] T011 [P] In `rankShippedFleet` (`RC`), set `hit` true when `shipped[0].skillId === hub` or `shipped[0].ownerSkillId === hub`, and set `present` true when any shipped entry has `skillId === hub` or `ownerSkillId === hub`. Change nothing else. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0 and prints `[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed`.\n \n ### Wave 2\n-- [ ] T012 In `D`, add `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)` and register `CA`'s `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `generatedSources`. Emit one `COMMAND_ROWS` row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry: its TypeScript id, its Python id and its entry id. `command` is the doctor runnable string from `DOCTOR_DETAILS` or the entry's `command`. `policy` is the `commandPolicies` record whose route matches the runnable's target, or the route-null record. When the runnable names no target and the command has several route records, take the strictest of `ask`, `start` and `run`. `ownerSkillId` is the entry's `skillId`. Emit `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string the same way. Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -n \"'command-doctor-update': \\{ command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'command-speckit-search': \\{ command: '/speckit:search', policy: 'run'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'create:agent': \\{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'\" $CA` prints one line and `$TC` exits 0.\n-- [ ] T013 [P] In `recommendationFromCli` (`FB`), keep `value.kind` when it is `skill` or `command` (default `skill`), keep `value.policy` when it is `run`, `start` or `ask`, and keep `value.ownerSkillId` when it is a non-empty string. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n-- [ ] T014 [P] In `$ADV/tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts`, add one case that parses a recommendation with all four fields and one that rejects it with `consequence: 'x'` added. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n-- [ ] T015 [P] In `RT`, add two cases through the stand-in advisor: a `create:agent` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` first and `sk-doc` second counts as a hit for `--hub sk-doc`, and a `command-doctor-git-hooks` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-git'` first and `sk-doc` second still prints `outranked`. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0.\n+- [x] T012 In `D`, add `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)` and register `CA`'s `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `generatedSources`. Emit one `COMMAND_ROWS` row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry: its TypeScript id, its Python id and its entry id. `command` is the doctor runnable string from `DOCTOR_DETAILS` or the entry's `command`. `policy` is the `commandPolicies` record whose route matches the runnable's target, or the route-null record. When the runnable names no target and the command has several route records, take the strictest of `ask`, `start` and `run`. `ownerSkillId` is the entry's `skillId`. Emit `COMMAND_POLICIES` keyed by runnable string the same way. Run `node $D`. Verify: `node $D --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, `rg -n \"'command-doctor-update': \\{ command: '/doctor:update', policy: 'ask'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'command-speckit-search': \\{ command: '/speckit:search', policy: 'run'\" $CA` prints one line, `rg -n \"'create:agent': \\{ command: '/create:agent', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'\" $CA` prints one line and `$TC` exits 0.\n+- [x] T013 [P] In `recommendationFromCli` (`FB`), keep `value.kind` when it is `skill` or `command` (default `skill`), keep `value.policy` when it is `run`, `start` or `ask`, and keep `value.ownerSkillId` when it is a non-empty string. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n+- [x] T014 [P] In `$ADV/tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts`, add one case that parses a recommendation with all four fields and one that rejects it with `consequence: 'x'` added. Verify: in `ADV`, `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed.\n+- [x] T015 [P] In `RT`, add two cases through the stand-in advisor: a `create:agent` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc'` first and `sk-doc` second counts as a hit for `--hub sk-doc`, and a `command-doctor-git-hooks` row with `ownerSkillId: 'sk-git'` first and `sk-doc` second still prints `outranked`. Verify: `node $RT` exits 0.\n \n ### Wave 3\n-- [ ] T016 In `publicRecommendation` (`H`), add `kind: recommendation.kind`, and when `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)` returns a row, add its `command`, its `policy` when present and its `ownerSkillId`. Verify: `$TC` exits 0, and after `npm run build` in `ADV`, `$REC '{\"prompt\":\"save context\"}' | jq '[.data.recommendations[] | select(.command == \"/speckit:save\")] | length'` prints 1.\n-- [ ] T017 In `R`, render the label of a recommendation that has a command, from its fields or else from `commandRowFor(skill)`, as `<ownerSkillId or skill> → <command> (<policy>)`, dropping the parenthesis when no policy is known. Use it for the `use` head and both sides of the `ambiguous` head. Every part passes `sanitizeSkillLabel`. Rewrite `doctorCommandString` to return `commandRowFor(id)?.command` for a doctor id. Leave the `Also:` line's trigger unchanged. Verify: `$TC` exits 0 and `rg -n \"DOCTOR_COMMAND_STRINGS\\[\" $R` prints nothing.\n-- [ ] T018 In `CLI`, pass the prompt to `degradedRecommendations` and export it. For an entry with a `commandRowFor(entry.skill)` row: when the prompt contains the row's bare slash command (the text before the first space), emit `skillId`, `kind: 'command'`, `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId`. Ot